Falsifies `pci::verification::the_message_signaled_interrupt_walk_terminates_on_any_device`.

The defect: the MSI walk's hop bound is raised from 64 to 65, the off-by-one a later edit that
"rounds the bound up to be safe" would make. The walk still terminates, but it reads one more
configuration dword than the contract the kernel's enumeration budget is written against.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(reads <= 66)`, on a device whose list never ends.

diff --git a/crates/pci/src/lib.rs b/crates/pci/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/pci/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/pci/src/lib.rs
@@ -689,7 +689,7 @@
         return None;
     }
     let mut at = (read32(bdf, CAPABILITIES_POINTER) & 0xfc) as u64;
-    for _ in 0..64 {
+    for _ in 0..65 {
         if at == 0 {
             return None;
         }
